# Defaults for nektos/act, which runs .github/workflows in Docker. Only lines
# starting with a dash are read as arguments, so the rest of this is comment.
#
#   act pull_request -j quality    # exactly what `just ci` runs, on a Linux runner
#   act pull_request -j test
#
# act otherwise picks a runner image interactively on first use and remembers
# the choice in ~/.actrc, which makes the image a property of whoever ran it.
# Pinning it here keeps every checkout on the same one, and this image carries
# the tooling jdx/mise-action expects to install onto.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# macos-latest and windows-latest are deliberately left unmapped, because
# mapping them at a Linux image would report a pass for a platform that never
# ran. The test matrix has three entries for a reason: several recipes have
# separate [unix] and [windows] bodies, and the Windows branch of `clean` is
# what that third entry exists to exercise.
#
# Note what act does with them: it prints "Skipping unsupported platform" and
# still exits 0. A green act run means Linux passed and says nothing at all
# about the other two -- only CI covers those.

# jdx/mise-action@v4 runs on node24. act 0.2.78 rejects that outright ("runs.using
# key in action.yml must be one of ... got node24") and never reaches the
# workflow; 0.2.89 runs it.
